---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy policy | Starlink Ghana Monitor" description="How the independent Starlink Ghana Monitor extension and calculator handle network readings, account information and device data." path="/privacy/">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 leading-relaxed">
    <a href="/" class="underline underline-offset-4">← Back to Starlink Ghana Monitor</a>
    <h1 class="mt-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mb-6 text-sm opacity-70">Last updated: 8 October 2026</p>
    <p>Starlink Ghana Monitor is an independent open-source tool built on Dishylink. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Starlink or SpaceX.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Local monitoring</h2>
    <p>While Chrome is running on your Starlink network, the extension reads connection performance, energy, outages and available router/device usage information. It saves recorded readings, cost assumptions and preferences in your browser. It does not read the pages you visit or send your recorded usage to our website.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Optional Starlink account</h2>
    <p>You can monitor your local network without signing in. If you connect your Starlink account, the extension reads your existing Starlink browser session and requests account, plan, billing, location and device information directly from Starlink. Account controls you use can change network settings. It retains a connection preference, not a permanent copy of your login cookies. The session may remain available in your ordinary Starlink browser login.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">External connections</h2>
    <p>Optional features can contact Starlink for account functions, CelesTrak for orbital data, Cloudflare for a speed test, our public website for version updates and GitHub for downloads. Hosts may receive standard connection metadata such as your IP address. The website calculator stores your inputs locally. You may choose to connect a separate local collector by providing its address.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Optional phone companion sync</h2>
    <p>The public <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/live/">phone companion</a> requires a private pairing link created by the laptop extension. If you opt in, the extension uploads aggregated traffic, energy, cost and recording freshness summaries approximately every ten minutes while Chrome runs. We store a hashed pairing credential and the latest summaries in Supabase PostgreSQL, not Starlink authentication cookies or individual device names. Anyone with your private pairing link can view those summaries. Disconnect from the extension to revoke the link and delete its cloud snapshot.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Your choices</h2>
    <p>You may decline optional location or account features, disconnect your Starlink account, and export your history and settings. Removing the extension or clearing its storage deletes locally recorded data unless you have exported a backup. Backups may contain sensitive usage patterns, so keep them private.</p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">Limited use and support</h2>
    <p>We use Chrome permissions to provide and improve the monitor's features, not for advertising or sale of user data. Use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy, including its Limited Use requirements.</p>
    <p>For a detailed explanation, read the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/hayalows/starlink/blob/master/PRIVACY.md">full privacy policy</a>. Contact the project through <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/hayalows/starlink/issues">GitHub Issues</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
